ubh|a|Finished; brought to perfection; refined; hence, free from impurity; excellent; superior; elegant; worthy of admiration; accomplished; beautiful. ; Aiming at show or effect; loaded with ornament; overdressed or overdecorated; showy. ; Nice; delicate; subtle; exquisite; artful; skillful; dexterous. ; Not coarse, gross, or heavy ; Not gross; subtile; thin; tenous. ; Not coarse; comminuted; in small particles; as, fine sand or flour. ; Not thick or heavy; slender; filmy; as, a fine thread. ; Thin; attenuate; keen; as, a fine edge. ; Made of fine materials; light; delicate; as, fine linen or silk. ; Having (such) a proportion of pure metal in its composition; as, coins nine tenths fine. ; (Used ironically.) ; To make fine; to refine; to purify, to clarify; as, to fine gold. ; To make finer, or less coarse, as in bulk, texture, etc.; as. to fine the soil. ; To change by fine gradations; as (Naut.), to fine down a ship's lines, to diminish her lines gradually.	j:1xxy,77,9;1lke,73,3;29r3,66,12;2bfb,65,73;ytb,62,6;2beo,58,41;nam,57,9;1lk0,57,12;1px0,48,6;1vsb,48,2;56m,45,40;18n,40,7;yfi,39,6;53w,37,30;1a21,33,124~1a21,33,124;1qwm,24,94;2bfb,65,73;l7d,21,54;2beo,58,41;56m,45,40;l79,31,39;53w,37,30;gqu,8,15;197m,11,13;6n6,26,12;1lk0,57,12;29b1,30,12;29r3,66,12;2fcw,8,11	e:1mkn,76,975;29xc,53,190;bx,38,86;17nk,34,1600;fix,29,106;rui,23,6;143q,18,5;1cde,15,2;1fc7,15,26;1qzq,15,131;t25,11,15;x7r,10,33;qur,8,11;cnj,7,25;1qri,4,6~17nk,34,1600;1mkn,76,975;29xc,53,190;1qzq,15,131;2epf,3,119;fix,29,106;bx,38,86;x7r,10,33;2dxk,0,31;1fc7,15,26;cnj,7,25;t25,11,15;qur,8,11;1qri,4,6;rui,23,6
